  "definition": "An artifact is 'Monetary High-Value' if its insurance value exceeds $1,000,000. It is 'Cultural/Historical High-Value' if its significance and cultural scores are in the top 10%. Otherwise, it is in the 'Other' category. This is derived from the 'High-Value Artifact' criteria."
